## ✅ PHASE 2 — Create the Dockerfile

### Step 2.1 — Create Dockerfile in your project

Create a file named **`Dockerfile`** (no extension!) in your project root:
`d:\MYCOMPANY\INSURANCE_PORTAL\Dockerfile`

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The filename must be exactly `Dockerfile` with capital D and no extension like `.txt`

Paste this content into the file:

```dockerfile
# ============================================================
# Stage 1: Build the JAR using Maven
# ============================================================
FROM maven:3.9.6-eclipse-temurin-17 AS builder

# Set working directory inside container
WORKDIR /app

# Copy pom.xml first (for dependency caching)
COPY pom.xml .

# Download all dependencies (cached layer)
RUN mvn dependency:go-offline -B

# Copy the rest of the source code
COPY src ./src

# Build the JAR (skip tests to speed up build)
RUN mvn clean package -DskipTests -B

# ============================================================
# Stage 2: Run the JAR in a lightweight image
# ============================================================
FROM eclipse-temurin:17-jre-jammy

# Set working directory
WORKDIR /app

# Copy only the built JAR from Stage 1
COPY --from=builder /app/target/insurance-portal-backend-1.0.0-SNAPSHOT.jar app.jar

# Expose the port your app runs on
EXPOSE 9191

# Run the application
ENTRYPOINT ["java", "-jar", "app.jar"]
```

---

### Step 2.2 — Create a `.dockerignore` file

Create a file named **`.dockerignore`** in your project root:
`d:\MYCOMPANY\INSURANCE_PORTAL\.dockerignore`

Paste this content:

```
target/
.git/
.gitignore
.settings/
.classpath
.project
*.md
```

> This tells Docker to ignore unnecessary files and makes the build faster.

