## ✅ PHASE 3 — Build & Test Locally

### Step 3.1 — Open Command Prompt in Your Project Folder

1. Open **File Explorer**
2. Go to `d:\MYCOMPANY\INSURANCE_PORTAL`
3. Click on the address bar, type `cmd`, press Enter
   *(This opens Command Prompt directly in your project folder)*

---

### Step 3.2 — Build the Docker Image

Run this command:
```bash
docker build -t insurance-portal:latest .
```

> [!NOTE]
> - `-t insurance-portal:latest` gives your image a name and tag
> - `.` means "use the Dockerfile in the current folder"
> - First run will take **5-10 minutes** (downloads Java + builds JAR). Subsequent builds are much faster.

You should see output ending with:
```
Successfully built xxxxxxxx
Successfully tagged insurance-portal:latest
```

---

### Step 3.3 — Test the App Locally with Docker

Run this command:
```bash
docker run -p 9191:9191 --name insurance-test insurance-portal:latest
```

> [!NOTE]
> - `-p 9191:9191` maps your PC's port 9191 to the container's port 9191
> - `--name insurance-test` gives the container a friendly name

Open your browser and go to:
```
http://localhost:9191/swagger-ui.html
```

If you see the Swagger UI — **your Docker image works perfectly!** 🎉

Stop the container when done:
```bash
docker stop insurance-test
docker rm insurance-test
```

