## ✅ PHASE 6 — Connect to Your EC2 Server

### Option A — Connect via AWS Console (Easiest — No Extra Tools Needed!)

1. Select your instance in EC2 → Click **"Connect"** button (top right)
2. Click **"EC2 Instance Connect"** tab
3. Click **"Connect"**
4. A browser terminal opens — you're now inside your server! ✅

### Option B — Connect via SSH from Windows (PowerShell)

1. Open **PowerShell** as Administrator
2. Run:
```powershell
ssh -i "C:\Users\kadam\Downloads\insurance-portal-key.pem" ubuntu@YOUR_EC2_IP
```
*(Replace `YOUR_EC2_IP` with your actual IP)*

If you get a permissions error, run this first:
```powershell
icacls "C:\Users\kadam\Downloads\insurance-portal-key.pem" /inheritance:r /grant:r "%USERNAME%:R"
```

