## ✅ PHASE 7 — Install Docker on EC2

Run these commands **one by one** in the EC2 terminal:

```bash
# Step 1: Update the server
sudo apt-get update -y

# Step 2: Install Docker
sudo apt-get install -y docker.io

# Step 3: Start Docker service
sudo systemctl start docker
sudo systemctl enable docker

# Step 4: Add your user to the docker group (so you don't need sudo)
sudo usermod -aG docker ubuntu

# Step 5: IMPORTANT — Log out and log back in for group change to take effect
exit
```

After running `exit`, reconnect to your server (repeat Step 6), then verify Docker:
```bash
docker --version
```
You should see: `Docker version 24.x.x` ✅

