## ✅ PHASE 8 — Transfer Your Docker Image to EC2

We have **two easy options**. Choose Option A (recommended for beginners):

---

### Option A — Use Docker Hub (Free & Easy) ⭐ RECOMMENDED

**On your Windows PC:**

**Step 8A.1 — Create Docker Hub account**
1. Go to: https://hub.docker.com/
2. Sign up for free
3. Your Docker Hub username will be something like `gaurav123`

**Step 8A.2 — Log in to Docker Hub on your PC**
```bash
docker login
```
Enter your Docker Hub username and password.

**Step 8A.3 — Tag and Push your image**
```bash
# Replace 'yourdockerhubusername' with YOUR actual Docker Hub username
docker tag insurance-portal:latest yourdockerhubusername/insurance-portal:latest
docker push yourdockerhubusername/insurance-portal:latest
```

Wait for the push to complete (2-5 minutes based on internet speed).

**On your EC2 server:**

**Step 8A.4 — Pull the image on EC2**
```bash
# Replace 'yourdockerhubusername' with YOUR Docker Hub username
docker pull yourdockerhubusername/insurance-portal:latest
```

---

### Option B — Build Directly on EC2 (No Docker Hub needed)

**Step 8B.1 — Install Git on EC2**
```bash
sudo apt-get install -y git
```

**Step 8B.2 — Clone your project on EC2**
```bash
git clone https://github.com/Gaurav-Coder7102/Insurance_Portal.git
cd Insurance_Portal
```

**Step 8B.3 — Install Maven on EC2**
```bash
sudo apt-get install -y maven
```

**Step 8B.4 — Build Docker image on EC2**
```bash
docker build -t insurance-portal:latest .
```
*(This will take 5-10 minutes)*

