## ✅ PHASE 9 — Run Your App on AWS! 🎉

### Step 9.1 — Start the Container

Run this command on your EC2 server:

```bash
docker run -d \
  -p 9191:9191 \
  --name insurance-portal \
  --restart always \
  insurance-portal:latest
```

> [!NOTE]
> - `-d` = run in background (detached mode)
> - `--restart always` = auto-restart if server reboots
> - `-p 9191:9191` = expose port 9191 to the internet

### Step 9.2 — Check if it's Running

```bash
docker ps
```

You should see your container listed with status `Up X seconds`.

### Step 9.3 — View Application Logs

```bash
docker logs insurance-portal
```

Look for: `Started InsurancePortalApplication in X.XXX seconds` ✅

### Step 9.4 — Access Your App on the Internet! 🌍

Open your browser and go to:
```
http://YOUR_EC2_IP:9191/swagger-ui.html
```
*(Replace `YOUR_EC2_IP` with your actual EC2 public IP)*

**You should see your Insurance Portal Swagger UI — Your app is LIVE on AWS! 🎉🎉🎉**

